  "About": {
    "h1": "About ",
    "span0": "ActuScientifique",
    "span1": "is an African",
    "span2": "science journalism",
    "p1": "media outlet dedicated to making science accessible to as many people as possible. The project was born from a simple observation: in Africa, much of the scientific information remains difficult for the general public to access, even though it is essential for understanding the world, making informed choices, and sustainably improving the well-being of populations.",
    "reading": "Read our editorial and commercial charter →",
    "engagement": "Our Commitment",
    "eVerb": "is committed to",
    "eSpan1": "transforming scientific research results into clear, reliable, and understandable information",
    "eLeftOver1": "tailored to African realities.",
    "eSpan2": "The media outlet is for everyone: citizens, students, professionals, decision-makers, and civil society actors.",
    "mission": "Our Mission",
    "mText": "To inform, explain, and educate the public on scientific topics of general interest, based on research data processed with rigor.",
    "ambition": "Our Ambition",
    "aText": "To contribute to the emergence of a strong scientific culture in Africa, capable of fighting disinformation and promoting evidence-based decisions.",
    "activities": "What We Do",
    "activitiesText": "Popularization,Decryption,Highlighting",
    "editorial": "Our Editorial Approach",
    "eTexts": "Reliability and verification,Clarity and pedagogy,Contextualization,Independence,Ethics",
    "why": "Why",
    "reasonP1": "Because science must not remain confined to laboratories. ",
    "reasonSpan": "It must be understood, embraced, and used by everyone.",
    "reasonP2": "By bringing science closer to citizens, we contribute to building better-informed African societies capable of meeting contemporary challenges.",
    "motto": "Science Journalism • Ethical • Independent"
